WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.335
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start position:0%
Welcome to
the "The Super Slow Show."

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.538 align:start position:0%
Dan, are you aware
of a website

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start position:0%
called 11foot8.com?

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.375 align:start position:0%
It's about this bridge
in North Carolina,

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.110 align:start position:0%
exactly 11 foot 8 inches
of clearance.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.678
- Who'da thought?
- For some reason,

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:15.281 align:start position:0%
people keep crashing
moving trucks into it,

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.251 size:75% position:38%
so frequently that a guy
has set up two cameras

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start position:0%
permanently recording
this bridge.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:53% position:47% line:0%
( tires screech )

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.228 align:start size:53% position:47%
( tires screech )

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:30.763 align:end position:100%
Today we're going to
recreate that experiment.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:33.266 align:start position:0%
- We have our own moving truck.
- Excellent name.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.601
<i> ( theme music playing )</i>

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:42.308
Well, not a great name
for a moving company, though,

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.210
especially if they charge
by the hour.

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:46.179
- Well, you'd make
 a lot of money.
- You would.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.315
Yeah, I'm kind of nervous about
driving a truck into a bridge.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:50.483 size:84% position:58%
And you don't drive at all.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.418 align:start position:0%
This is true.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.521 align:end position:100%
Which is why we've got
our very own stunt driver,
Kyle.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:56.823
Afternoon,
Kyle the stunt driver.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.524
- Good afternoon.
- How's it going?

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:02.261
This is our bridge.
It's not actually a bridge.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:04.197 align:end position:100%
Dan:
Yeah, it's also not 11' 8".

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.200 align:start position:0%
But it will be solid impact
for a truck.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.734 align:end position:100%
I should think so,
which I why I'm scared of it.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.203 align:end position:100% line:0%
Have you done anything
like this before,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.704 size:84% position:58% line:0%
like running into a bridge?

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.673 align:start position:0% line:0%
You know, thankfully, I've never
run into a bridge before.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.707 line:0%
- No?
- No.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:15.708 align:start size:66% position:34%
You nervous about it?

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.477
No, not too really.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.245
I'm definitely interested
to find out what happens.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:20.646
It's kind of scary

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.648
because a lot of the trucks
just stop dead.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.784
It's like actually crashing
into a wall almost.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.853
- Yeah, it's interesting.
- Are you prepared
  for a sudden impact

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.654 align:end position:100%
just in case it doesn't
tear the top off?

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:30.823 align:start position:0%
Yeah, yeah, I've got a
five-point harness system
in there.

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.291 align:start position:0%
I should be good to go,

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:35.661 align:start position:0%
even coming from
a 35-mile-an hour truck,

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start position:0%
coming to a dead stop,
I think.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.464 align:end position:100%
Is that how fast
you're going?

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start position:0%
Yeah, 30, 35.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.734 align:end position:100%
I still wouldn't want to be
doing this myself.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.903 size:88% position:56%
I'm so glad that we've got
you to do this instead.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.671 align:start position:0%
Hopefully it just peels
the lid right off.

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:46.772
That's the effect we want.

00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:47.874
- Kyle: That's the plan.
- Yeah.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.375 align:start position:0%
All right, well,
from this point on

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:51.144 size:88% position:44%
the video's in your hands.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.514
Yeah, I guess we're just gonna
radio and just go, "Go!"

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.149
- And then that's it for us.
- That's it, yeah.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.450
- It's all on you.
- Great. Good luck, Kyle.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.818
Thank you.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.586
- Dan: Cool.
- Gav: Let's get to safety.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start position:0%
See you guys
on the other side.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.525 align:start position:0%
We're going to record this
at a thousand frames a second,
in 4K,

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.826 size:81% position:41%
one camera looking down,

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.662 align:start position:0%
one looking right
at the point of impact.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.497
- Are you ready?
- I'm ready.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.933
- Let's hope Kyle's ready.
- Okay.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.269
Kyle, go, go, go!

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start position:0%
Gav ( laughing ):
It's so scary to look at.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:21.841 align:end position:100%
Dan:
Oh, I can't wait already.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
Oh, he's bookin' it.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:91% position:9%
He really is.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:25.612 align:start size:78% position:22%
He's really going for it.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.551
( together )
Ooh!

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.587
( laughing )
Oh!

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.621 align:start size:31% position:69%
Dan: Damn!

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:97% position:3%
It completely split.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.960
Look, it's literally like
the top of a can. Isn't it?

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.563 align:end position:100%
It ripped the top off
and then snapped the back.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.531 align:end position:100%
Dan:
It's completely wrinkled.

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:25% position:75%
Oh, man.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:50.903 align:end position:100%
I didn't realize they made
convertible trucks.

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:53.372
Properly, like,
accordioned it.

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:55.508
It's actually, I think,

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.444
- got inside the container.
- Oh.

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.313 align:start size:69% position:31%
Oh, look at the truck.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.281 align:start size:44% position:56%
Here it comes.

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:03.850 align:start size:72% position:28%
That's fully opened up.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.926
- Gav: Well done.
- Dan: How was that?

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.595
Well, I felt a bit of a bump.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.263
- You did?
- Is that it?
  Just a bit of a bump?

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:18.364 align:start size:72% position:28%
Just a bit of an "unh."

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.433
And look what you've done.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.602 align:end position:100%
Well, there's your problem.
Your roof's up there.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.503
Gav:
Can you see that it's
actually embedded itself

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:26.239
in the shipping container
material?

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.708 align:end position:100%
Yeah, I might've-- might've
drifted up towards 40

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.509 align:start size:69% position:31%
right before I hit it.

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:31.944
You weren't messing around.
You were like, wow.

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:33.579 align:start size:59% position:41%
Lead foot, I guess.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.915 align:start position:0%
Why don't we go and see
what the hell just happened?

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:38.251
- In slow mo.
- Yeah, that'd be great.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.421
Oh, there's the shadow.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.462
<i> ( all laughing )</i>

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.631
Gav: <i> It's just driving
 into itself.</i>

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.299
<i> It's folding itself up.</i>

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:54.767
Dan: <i> It's, like, using it up,
 isn't it?</i>

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.902
<i> That bar
 didn't actually crumple.</i>

00:03:56.935 --> 00:04:00.539 align:start position:0%
- Kyle: <i> No. </i>
- Gav: <i> That bar went
all the way in that top part.</i>

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.576 size:88% position:44%
<i>Oh, now you're just dragging
 the... ( laughing )</i>

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:04.810 align:start size:63% position:38%
Dan: <i> I feel like
 it's not so much--</i>

00:04:04.843 --> 00:04:06.445 align:start size:72% position:28%
<i> 'cause it's only 8'6".</i>

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:07.947 align:start size:63% position:38%
<i> It's not so much
 shaved the top off</i>

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.382 align:start size:59% position:41%
<i> as decapitated it
 completely.</i>

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start position:0%
What you've done there,

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.451 size:84% position:42%
you've made very hard metal

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:13.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
look like cloth.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:15.855
It's amazing what
high speeds will do 

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.924
to hard materials.

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:22.528
<i> You know, just out
 for a Sunday drive.</i>

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.464
<i> Nothing out of the normal.</i>

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:28.834 align:start position:0% line:0%
Oh, the ripple
through that.

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.336 size:75% position:38% line:0%
That's wicked.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.672 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's like that scene
in "Willy Wonka"

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start position:0% line:0%
where it goes in dirty
and comes out clean

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.377 align:start position:0% line:0%
except this comes out
without a roof.

00:04:38.877 --> 00:04:40.746 align:start position:0%
Dan: <i> Now it's just convertible.
It's just gone.</i>

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start position:0%
Gav: <i> That is amazing.</i>

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:43.549
Kyle: <i> Now it's more
 of a flatbed truck.</i>

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.718 align:start position:0%
Gav:
<i>Yeah. Still functional.</i>

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:48.020 align:start position:0%
<i>Still runs.</i>

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:51.724 align:start position:0%
<i>( laughing )
Did you see the text
on the side?</i>

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.392 align:start size:69% position:31%
Dan: <i> Oh, it's just
 squashed completely.</i>

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:54.560
<i> so it says "Mo-ers" instead.</i>

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:56.429 align:start position:0%
<i>That is absolutely
crumpled.</i>

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.997
Kyle: <i> Yeah, the accordion
 effect's amazing.</i>

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.565 align:start size:66% position:34%
<i> It's like a cartoon.</i>

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.033 align:start size:56% position:44%
<i> It was just like
 a cartoon crash.</i>

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.102
- Just, like, perfect folds.
- Yeah.

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start position:0%
I want to see
the other side of the container

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.440
because that bar went in
so deep.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.674
- Yeah.
- Should we go check it out?

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.076
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:11.543 --> 00:05:13.713
Oh!
What?

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
It came fully out
the other side.

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:17.516 align:start size:75% position:25%
Dan: That's so abstract.

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start position:0%
Gav:
So it looks like it's
bonked that side.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.354
It actually pierced this side.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.022
- Dan: Oh, yeah.
- Kyle: Just punched
  straight through.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.523
- Huh.
- Huh.

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:25.891
- Um.
- Great.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.460
- Do you wanna do it again?
- Yeah. Yep.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.128 align:start size:31% position:69%
All right.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:30.763 align:start position:0%
So, second attempt.

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.932 align:start position:0%
I wonder if he's going
to make it through

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.434 align:start position:0%
the exact same holes
as last time.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.569 size:84% position:58%
That'll be damn impressive.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.870
Do you think he could go?

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.071 align:end position:100%
I'm not even sure
this truck's the same width.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.139 align:start size:66% position:34%
All right, we'll see.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.007 align:start position:0%
Yeah. All right, okay,
you ready?

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.843
- I'm ready.
- Okay.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.446
All right, Kyle,
we're ready for you.
Go! Go! Go!

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.850 align:end position:100%
Gav:
This one sounds
a little bit more rickety.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.552 align:start position:0%
Dan:
It does, doesn't it?

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.824
- Getting up to some
  serious speed now.
- Really is.

00:05:58.857 --> 00:06:01.527 align:start position:0%
Good night!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.729
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.531
What was that?

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.099 align:end position:100%
It has gone
through the same holes!

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:09.668
- ( Gav laughs )
- I knew it!

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:12.104 align:start position:0%
It literally did exactly
what you said.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:15.541
- I called it.
- And that one exploded.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:17.643 align:end position:100%
Was that a real moving truck?
Was there stuff in it?

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:18.978 align:start position:0%
That one was insolated.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.680
- That was
  a refrigeration truck.
- Oh...

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:23.849 align:end position:100%
I wondered whether
you'd be able to get it

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:26.152 align:end position:100%
through the exact same holes
as you did last time.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:29.054 align:end position:100%
You're that good
that you nailed it perfectly.

00:06:29.087 --> 00:06:31.424 align:start size:81% position:19%
So this one was insulated.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.927 align:start position:0%
Yeah, I think they turned
this one into a refrigerated
box truck.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.729
Yeah, look at this.

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.664
I was like, "What's with that
gunk that's falling out of it?"

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:40.800
That one was like an explosion.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.002 align:end position:100%
It was completely different
because the other one
just peeled away.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:45.004 align:start size:56% position:44%
<i> This one sort of
 exploded almost.</i>

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.006
Should we go and check out some
of the carnage underneath?

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.442 align:start position:0%
Dan:
There's more carnage
this time, almost.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:50.709 align:end position:100%
Kyle:
Ooh, lots of debris.

00:06:50.742 --> 00:06:52.077 align:start size:59% position:41%
Peeling off nicely.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.212
Kyle, you broke the sign.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:54.613 align:start position:0%
Oh, no.

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:55.815 size:88% position:56%
Now it's just "Low Clear..."

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.116 align:start position:0%
Yeah.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:59.685 align:end position:100%
That is mental.
Look at that shot.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:01.220 align:start size:41% position:59%
That is cool.

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:02.922
You go faster or slower
on that one?

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:05.458 align:start position:0%
I think it was actually
pretty much about the same,

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:06.859 align:start position:0%
pretty close to 40.

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:14.900 align:start position:0%
 Gav:
<i>Whoa, it's spewing out
the sides.</i>

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:17.470 align:end position:100%
 Dan: <i> Look at the sides there,
 all the foam coming
 out the sides.</i>

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.605
Kyle ( laughing ):
<i> Look at the top corner.</i>

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:21.006 align:start size:28% position:72%
<i> Oh, man.</i>

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:25.244 align:start position:0%
<i>That is mental.
Look at all that.</i>

00:07:25.277 --> 00:07:27.746 align:start size:53% position:47%
<i> I wouldn't hire
 this company.</i>

00:07:27.779 --> 00:07:29.482 align:start size:31% position:69%
<i> For sure.</i>

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.651
<i> - If that was your stuff?
 - </i> Gav: <i> No.</i>

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.758
Kyle:
<i> Jeez, look at all
 that stuff flying.</i>

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:43.662 align:start size:81% position:19%
 Dan:
<i> Then the roof falls down
 behind it as well.</i>

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:45.498
<i> That's such a weird sight,</i>

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.533 align:start position:0%
<i>like I barely know
what I'm looking at.</i>

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:50.703 align:start position:0%
<i>- Looks like--
- Look at all that peeling out
 on the left.</i>

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.671
<i> A refrigerated sheep holder.</i>

00:07:52.704 --> 00:07:53.739 align:start position:0%
<i>It does look like--</i>

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:54.807 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> It's almost just like...</i>

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.175 align:start position:0%
<i>A sheep popped.</i>

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.911 align:start size:69% position:31%
<i> Yeah, it really does.</i>

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:00.847 align:start position:0%
<i>That's a great shot.
That's cool.</i>

00:08:06.818 --> 00:08:10.823 align:start position:0%
<i>Here we go.
Look at this slot
perfectly in there.</i>

00:08:10.856 --> 00:08:15.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> - </i> Dan: <i> Gosh.
 - </i> Gav: <i> Straight
 through the holes!</i>

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:17.830 size:78% position:39%
<i> It's just peeling off.</i>

00:08:17.863 --> 00:08:19.965 align:start size:66% position:34%
<i> Look at all that
 coming out the top,
 the carnage there.</i>

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:21.734
Kyle:
<i> It just accordions
 that sheet metal up top.</i>

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.136 align:start position:0%
<i>It really does.</i>

